cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Local Digital Visibility Index
message: >-
  If you use this dataset or reproduce these figures, please cite it. The
  published analysis lives at hub.pyc.agency/indices; this repository holds
  the open data and the pipeline that produced it.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Yarrow
    given-names: Phil
    affiliation: PYC
    website: https://pyc.agency
repository-code: https://github.com/philyarrow/local-digital-visibility-index
url: https://hub.pyc.agency/indices/
abstract: >-
  Quarterly league tables scoring South West UK businesses 0-100 on a Digital
  Visibility Score, built from six weighted pillars: Speed and Core Web Vitals,
  Technical foundation, Local presence, Visibility, AI search presence, and
  Content and trust. Q3-2026 covers 271 businesses across 11 indices in Bath,
  Bristol, Cheltenham, Exeter, Gloucester, Swindon and Worcester. Every score is
  recomputable from the published data using the pipeline in this repository.
  Superseded snapshots are retained alongside each release, so any previously
  cited figure remains recoverable.
keywords:
  - local-seo
  - open-data
  - core-web-vitals
  - digital-visibility
  - south-west-england
  - ai-search
license: CC-BY-4.0
version: q3-2026
date-released: '2026-08-30'
